
Executive Summary
AirtelBlack.com is a statically-hosted single-page website (Satirical “Airtel Blackout”) that mimics Airtel’s branding and UX to lampoon its customer service. The site uses custom HTML/CSS/JavaScript without any heavy frameworks: it is hosted on Cloudflare Pages (static) and built “manually,” but with professional polish. Key techniques include dark-theme CSS with the Inter font, CSS animations and IntersectionObserver-based scroll effects, animated counters, and an interactive Bingo game using browser localStorage. It even autoplays the Airtel jingle on loop via an audio element. The markup uses semantic tags (skip-links, headings, sections, FAQ schema) for SEO and accessibility. No JS frameworks or analytics were detected; it appears to be mostly vanilla JS (with modern browser APIs) and all assets are static. We confirmed these traits via site content and secondary reports (e.g. Adeesh Sharma’s analysis).

Key findings (detailed below) include:

Site Architecture: Single HTML with anchor navigation; splash screen on load; sections (Services, CEO letter, RFCs, Wall, Bingo, etc.). Uses <nav>, <main>, <section>, <footer> semantically (e.g. “Skip to main content” link at top).
CSS: Fully custom, dark theme with Airtel red accents. Uses Google’s Inter font. Employs CSS animations (fade-in, transitions) and responsive design (likely flexbox/grid). No Bootstrap/Tailwind was detected; styling is handcrafted.
JS: Pure JavaScript. Uses IntersectionObserver for scroll-triggered reveals, a scripted counter (clock/counters) and “damage bar,” and a custom bingo minigame (clickable cells with localStorage persistence). It autoplays audio (Airtel jingle) and handles a clickable “coffee mug” link (mailto: wesuck@airtelblack.com) for visitor feedback. A JSON-LD <script> for FAQ schema (SEO) is included.
Build/Deployment: Hosted on Cloudflare Pages (static). Likely authored as simple HTML/CSS/JS, possibly bundled/minified by a tool (Webpack/Rollup or none) before upload.
Other: No analytics or trackers seen. Uses localStorage (no cookies) for state. Fast load (assets small, minified). SSL and security via Cloudflare. The site uses SEO best-practices (meta tags, FAQ schema) and has accessible features (skip-nav).
